-       Inside an `inline` method the check is deferred to the expansion site, where the
-       type parameter is concrete, so `inline def f[value: Concrete]` compiles and each
-       call to it is checked. `Concrete.apply[self]()` makes an instance by hand, for a
-       macro which has established the fact itself.
-   entry .concrete   the macro given: `typeRef is Concrete` when the type is not abstract
-   entry .apply   an instance by assertion: `Concrete[self]()`
+       Dentro de un método `inline`, la comprobación se aplaza al punto de expansión, donde el
+       parámetro de tipo es concreto, de modo que `inline def f[value: Concrete]` compila y se
+       comprueba cada llamada a él. `Concrete.apply[self]()` crea una instancia a mano, para una
+       macro que ya ha establecido el hecho por sí misma.
+   entry .concrete   el given macro: `typeRef is Concrete` cuando el tipo no es abstracto
+   entry .apply   una instancia por afirmación: `Concrete[self]()`

- entry .Distinct   the proof that a type is not a member of a union: `self is Distinct from union`
+ entry .Distinct   la prueba de que un tipo no es miembro de una unión: `self is Distinct from union`

= entry .Distinct   the proof that a type is not a member of a union: `self is Distinct from union`
-   detail
+   detail

-       `typeRef is Distinct from otherType` is produced by the inline given `.distinct`, a
-       macro which first requires `typeRef` to be `Concrete` (error `↯/s.20.5` otherwise) and then
-       fails with error `↯/s.20.2`, _type `typeRef` cannot be proven distinct from `otherType`_,
-       when `typeRef` is a subtype of `otherType`. It is the check which keeps `Unset` out
-       of a value type, and it lets an API accept "one or several" without ambiguity:
-       caduceus's `many[entity: Distinct from List[Any]](value: entity | List[entity])`
-       can tell a single element from a list of them only because `entity` is proven not
-       to be a list itself.
+       `typeRef is Distinct from otherType` lo produce el given inline `.distinct`, una macro
+       que primero exige que `typeRef` sea `Concrete` (error `↯/s.20.5` en otro caso) y después
+       falla con el error `↯/s.20.2`, _type `typeRef` cannot be proven distinct from
+       `otherType`_, cuando `typeRef` es un subtipo de `otherType`. Es la comprobación que
+       mantiene `Unset` fuera de un tipo de valor, y permite que una API acepte «uno o varios»
+       sin ambigüedad: el `many[entity: Distinct from List[Any]](value: entity | List[entity])`
+       de caduceus puede distinguir un único elemento de una lista de ellos solo porque se ha
+       demostrado que `entity` no es a su vez una lista.

=       to be a list itself.
