- entry .Mandatable   the non-optional type a present value has: `self is Mandatable to result`
+ entry .Mandatable   el tipo no opcional que tiene un valor presente: `self is Mandatable to result`

= entry .Mandatable   the non-optional type a present value has: `self is Mandatable to result`
-   detail
+   detail

-       `typeRef is Mandatable` is produced by the transparent inline given `.mandatable`, a
-       macro which strips every `Unset` from a union type and records what is left as its
-       `#Result`: `Optional[Text] is Mandatable to Text`. A type with no `Unset` in it fails
-       with error `↯/s.20.1`, _the value is not an `Optional`_. Derivation code uses it to find the
-       type to encode or render for an optional field — breviloquence's CBOR encoder and the
-       derived `Inspectable` both take `[inner <: value, value >: Unset.type: Mandatable to
-       inner]`.
-   entry .mandatable   the macro given: `typeRef is Mandatable to result`, with the `Unset` removed
-   entry .apply   an instance by assertion: `Mandatable[self, result]()`
-   entry #Result   the type with optionality removed; a subtype of `Self`
+       `typeRef is Mandatable` lo produce el given transparent inline `.mandatable`, una macro
+       que elimina cada `Unset` de un tipo unión y registra lo que queda como su `#Result`:
+       `Optional[Text] is Mandatable to Text`. Un tipo sin ningún `Unset` falla con el error
+       `↯/s.20.1`, _the value is not an `Optional`_. El código de derivación lo usa para
+       encontrar el tipo que se ha de codificar o representar para un campo opcional: tanto el
+       codificador CBOR de breviloquence como el `Inspectable` derivado toman
+       `[inner <: value, value >: Unset.type: Mandatable to inner]`.
+   entry .mandatable   el given macro: `typeRef is Mandatable to result`, sin el `Unset`
+   entry .apply   una instancia por afirmación: `Mandatable[self, result]()`
+   entry #Result   el tipo sin la opcionalidad; un subtipo de `Self`

- entry .Extractor   a pattern extractor which answers with an `Optional`
+ entry .Extractor   un extractor de patrones que responde con un `Optional`

= entry .Extractor   a pattern extractor which answers with an `Optional`
-   detail
+   detail

-       A trait for an object meant to be used in `case Name(value) =>` patterns: implement
-       `#extract`, returning an `Optional[extraction]`, and `#unapply` is derived from it as
-       the `Option` the pattern matcher requires. `Uuid` and phoenicia's `Otf` are
-       `Extractor[Text, …]`, so `case Uuid(uuid) =>` matches text that parses as one.
+       Un trait para un objeto pensado para usarse en patrones `case Name(value) =>`: se
+       implementa `#extract`, que devuelve un `Optional[extraction]`, y `#unapply` se deriva
+       de él como el `Option` que exige el comparador de patrones. `Uuid` y el `Otf` de
+       phoenicia son `Extractor[Text, …]`, de modo que `case Uuid(uuid) =>` reconoce un texto
+       que se analiza como tal.

=       `Extractor[Text, …]`, so `case Uuid(uuid) =>` matches text that parses as one.
